    <h3 id="energy">Home energy and storm resilience</h3>
    <p>Winter Storm Uri in 2021 and Hurricane Beryl's long Houston outages in 2024 pushed thousands of homeowners to buy generators, batteries and solar. That created steady work for installer helpers, electricians' assistants, generator maintenance and solar sales. Licensed trades earn the most; helpers and site-survey roles are open to beginners.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $18–$40/hr; licensed trades more</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Tools, training</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Hands-on workers</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="construction">Construction and home services</h3>
    <p>New subdivisions keep going up around Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, Austin and San Antonio. New homeowners need fences stained, garages organized, furniture assembled, gutters cleaned and driveways pressure washed. Weekend handyman work is one of the best-paying hustles per hour in the state.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $35–$75/hr</li><li><b>Startup:</b> $200–$800 in tools</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Weekends</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="events">Events and festivals</h3>
